Z||000000||Banzai||09-07-2001||08:46 AM||||Has  anyone done or heard  of a 4.3 Vortec swap being done. Should adapt similarly to the 350. I'm just curious. My 95 truck and van both have this motor and it moves those rolling bricks pretty good.<P>Banzai !!!!!!!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000001||Raydar||09-07-2001||09:07 AM||||It's been done, but it's not too common. Try running a search on 4.3. It requires the same trans adapter as a V-8. General consensus is that if you're gonna go to all that trouble, go for the V-8. If you want a big 90* V-6, the 3800 is easier. No trans adapter is required, and in SC form they make a ton of power.<BR>I had considered this swap at one time. I have a 4.3 in my Sonoma, and it could almost drag my house out into the yard.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Raydar - aka Steve<BR><FONT SIZE="1"><BR>Black 88 Formula.<BR>Red 88 Duke coupe. "The Project" <BR>88 Formula parts car. "The Donor"<BR></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||FieroBUZZ||09-07-2001||09:45 AM||||I see an advantage with insurance and registration as your car would still be a six cylinder as per 'stock' specs.  However with the work involved, a 3800 does seem to be a more sensible swap.<P>I have the 4.3 in my 97 Jimmy and love the motor.<P>Gary<BR>86 SE||||reg||12
